00:02:00.500 --> 00:02:09.000
Sarah Jenkins: Completely agree, David. Centralized identity lifecycle management is crucial for enterprise-grade SOC2 compliance. What timeline does your team need for that?

00:02:09.500 --> 00:02:22.000
David Sterling: This brings us to Section 5.3 in the contract. Our enterprise fiscal year kickoff is in May. Our internal rollout across the 250 named engineers is strictly slated for May 15th.

00:02:22.500 --> 00:02:35.000
Sarah Jenkins: Okay, so if we deliver the SAML SSO gateway before May, that gives your team two weeks for staging validation and user acceptance testing.

00:02:35.500 --> 00:02:48.000
David Sterling: Exactly. But here is the hard line from our VP of Procurement and Legal: We need Section 5.3 to explicitly define a hard delivery deadline of May 1st for custom SAML 2.0 and SCIM directory synchronization.

00:02:48.500 --> 00:03:02.000
Sarah Jenkins: Understood. Let me confirm the exact wording with Dr. Elena Rostova, our CTO, and Alex Vance, our CEO. From our side, May 1st gives us roughly seven months to build and harden the connector.

00:03:02.500 --> 00:03:16.000
David Sterling: Good. Now Sarah, I have to emphasize the legal consequence clause we drafted into Section 5.3: If SAML SSO is not delivered by May 1st, Acme Corp will cancel the $80,000 ARR pilot contract.

00:03:16.500 --> 00:03:28.000
Sarah Jenkins: Understood. So if we hit May 1st without production-ready SAML and SCIM, Acme Corp exercises immediate unilateral cancellation with a 100% refund of prepaid fees.

00:03:28.500 --> 00:03:42.000
David Sterling: That is the exact condition. If you miss May 1st, we pull the plug. We cannot deploy software to 250 engineers that operates outside our Okta perimeter. But if you hit May 1st, this expands to 1,000 seats in Year 2.

00:03:42.500 --> 00:03:55.000
Sarah Jenkins: That expansion potential is massive for us, David. That would make Acme Corp our largest flagship customer by far. I am logging this commitment directly into our system right now.

00:03:55.500 --> 00:04:10.000
